WEBVTT

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:14.900
Excuse me, officer.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:15.730
Can you help me?

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:16.970
Sure.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:17.660
Can you tell me

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.120
how to get to Linden Street, in Riverdale?

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.190
"Richard Stewart, 46 Linden Street,

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.580
Riverdale, New York."

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.350
You should take the number 1 subway.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.770
Is there a station near here?

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:28.730
Yes. The station's that way.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:29.900
You should take the number 1 train

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.240
to Van Cortlandt Park.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.450
Number 1 train to Van Cortlandt Park. Thank you.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:35.650
Anytime. Good luck.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:39.070
Remember, the number 1 train. The uptown platform.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:59.400
Thank you.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.090
Is this pink too bright for me?

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:10.450
Mmm-hmm. It is a very bright pink.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:14.750
Try this. It's size eight.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.710
But I wear size ten.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:21.570
How about green? It's size ten.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.370
Let me try it on.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:30.020
I'm taking too much of your time.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:31.170
It's six o'clock.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.910
Where's my husband?

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.990
I was expecting him here at five forty-five.

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:37.420
Don't worry. The traffic is very heavy at this hour.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:41.950
I know. But we're going to be late for dinner.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.450
I'll take this green sweater.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.990
I like the color on me, don't you?

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:52.470
I think it looks terrific on you.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.620
I'm sorry I'm so late.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:56.430
I had a really bad day.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.700
It's ten after six. We're late.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:00.700
Robbie's cooking tonight, and dinner's at six thirty.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:03.890
I know. I know. I'm really sorry.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.310
I left my bag of film on the ferry.

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:08.230
I went back for it, but the ferry was gone.

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:10.580
I lost a whole day's work.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.340
I'll call the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:21.570
I didn't think of that. Thanks.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.610
Hello.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:24.570
Yes. The number, please,

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:29.640
of the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:35.670
Five five five...zero eight zero eight.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.380
Thank you.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:40.680
I really appreciate it, Marilyn.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.140
Hello.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.760
Did anyone find a camera bag this afternoon,

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:49.180
a small canvas bag,

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:55.940
on the J. F. Kennedy Ferry?...No?

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.130
Maybe someone will find it.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:01.320
The name is Stewart, Richard Stewart.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:04.820
And the telephone number is five five five...

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:11.120
three oh nine oh. Thank you.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.350
Sorry, Richard. They don't have it.

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:18.750
Thanks, anyway.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.290
There was a girl on the ferry.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.020
Now maybe...

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.940
Tell me about it on the way home.
